<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NS - no seller T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH		PREV</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	    15/10 D	 April	     15/10 D</p>
<p> May		15/10 D	 May		 15/10 D</p>
<p> July	    even/6 P	 July	     even/6 P</p>
<p> August	   15/20 P	 August	    15/20 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	     10/5 D	 March		 9/3 D</p>
<p> May		14/13 D	 May		 14/13 D</p>
<p> July	     17/15 D	 July		16/15 D</p>
<p> August	     7/4 D	 August		6/4 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	    75/50 D	 April	     75/60 D</p>
<p> May	    140/110 D	 May	     140/115 D</p>
<p> July	   160/130 D	 July	    150/130 D</p>
<p> August	 160/130 D	 August	  150/130 D</p>
<p>Note: There will be no price messages on March 27 and 28 due to the Easter holiday. The next price message will be on March 31.</p>
